<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Matilda I, Countess of Boulogne</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1105–<a href="/years/1152">1152</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Matilda of Boulogne</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Matilda I, Countess of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boulogne-sur-mer">Boulogne</a>, held the county in her own right from 1125 and, as wife of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stephen-king-of-england">Stephen of Blois</a>, was queen of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> from 1135. During the civil war known as the Anarchy she defended her husband's cause, raising troops in Kent and securing his release after his capture at Lincoln in 1141. Her son Eustace was Stephen's heir but died before him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/matilda-i-countess-of-boulogne.jpg" alt="Matilda I, Countess of Boulogne" width="175" height="172" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Robert Withy, John Ryall · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coin_of_Stephen_of_Blois_and_Matilda_of_Boulogne_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
